            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I can not reproduce.\r\n\r\nWhat I did was set up bare minimum:\r\n- '.config/nvim/init.lua' with this code:\r\n\r\n    ```lua\r\n    local lazypath = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/lazy/lazy.nvim\"\r\n    if not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n      vim.fn.system({\r\n        \"git\",\r\n        \"clone\",\r\n        \"--filter=blob:none\",\r\n        \"https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git\",\r\n        \"--branch=stable\", -- latest stable release\r\n        lazypath,\r\n      })\r\n    end\r\n    vim.opt.rtp:prepend(lazypath)\r\n    \r\n    require(\"lazy\").setup(\"plugins\")\r\n    ```\r\n- '.config/nvim/lua/plugins/starter.lua' with the code copied from this issue.\r\n\r\nRan it first time - installed 'lazy.nvim' and 'mini.starter'. Ran it second time - got welcoming 'mini.starter' screen.\r\n\r\nCan this be due to some plugin setup collision using 'lazy.nvim'? Did you try making as clean install as possible?",
